{"id": "EUVD-2026-88738", "enisaUuid": "faae9c87-9a15-3777-96e3-707bb0f772ad", "description": "Apache XmlSchema doesn't limit how deeply schema structures can be nested when it builds its schema model, so a malicious schema can make parsing recurse until the stack overflows. This causes a denial of service.\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 2.3.3, which fixes this issue.", "datePublished": "2026-09-29T11:34:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-29T20:12:07", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://lists.apache.org/thread/9z1vg8wmvwpfw748fb2nb55w4hgbnxol"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-102496", "GHSA-jp7g-xv94-gfw8"], "assigner": "apache", "epss": 0.53, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "80991819-412e-3617-8d97-b3d1d5f9a2d7", "product": {"name": "Apache XMLSchema", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.3.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d91bb8e5-1b04-38ac-9165-07f20507d4d4", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}